{
  "A": "Develop the compact serial selector from 0616d195a8be4e58 as a low-overhead alternative to C. Retain its exact k=1 path and packed distance/group records; evaluate adding C's nearest-versus-farthest complement selection and histogram voting separately. Use bottom-up heap initialization and storage proportional to min(k,N-k) for 0<k<N. Prove that group ordinal can replace encounter index for the output label: equal-distance points within one group are interchangeable, but ties across groups must preserve traversal priority, reversed for exclusions. Handle k>=N through all labels plus any placeholder votes. Preserve the reference fallback for unordered distances. Deliver independently measured variants rather than assuming compact records, complement selection and histogram voting have additive benefits.",
  "B": "Redirect SIMD research away from the O(Nk) insertion-position scan. Investigate guarded ARM64 NEON batches for distance calculation and conservative heap-threshold rejection on the improved selection algorithm. Process surviving candidates in encounter order; a threshold captured before a batch may admit extra candidates but must never discard one that could enter the final selection. Treat nearest and farthest tie rules separately, and detect NaNs even in rejected batches before invoking reference fallback. Match the existing compiled scalar distance arithmetic, including rounding and contraction; neither introduce nor remove fused operations silently. Retain scalar tails and portable fallback. Measure this kernel against the same heap implementation without SIMD.",
  "C": "Use c2ee9f2bc1084b39 as the incumbent parallel design. Investigate whether team startup, private-heap storage and final candidate merging justify fewer workers for particular general N and m=min(k,N-k) regimes. Keep balanced contiguous ranges, at most four workers, and serial execution when OpenMP is unavailable or parallel work is insufficient. Bound each local heap by min(m,range_length), and preserve deterministic global selection when merging. Compare serial and parallel variants with otherwise identical selection and voting to isolate threading effects. Incorporate A's compact records only as a separately measured experiment after its tie-equivalence proof. Avoid shared heap updates and subtract only globally selected exclusions from the all-label histogram.",
  "G": "Start from the complete c2ee9f2bc1084b39 program at commit 97642630fa7d76c1ffd8f3fd16191542f27e724a, retaining it unchanged as the fallback incumbent. The displayed diffs are truncated and overlap src/knn.c, so integrate complete implementations semantically rather than concatenating patches. First evaluate A's exact k=1 path and compact records independently; then consider C's scheduling refinement and B's SIMD kernel only when their correctness and measurements justify inclusion. Use one consistent tie policy, NaN fallback and histogram ordering throughout. Recheck correctness and measure every integrated candidate through the unchanged harness within existing budgets. Compare against both the incumbent and contributing standalone programs; reject regressions and do not require contributions from every tree. Preserve parsing, output format, compiler, target, tests and oracle.",
  "analysis": "The task is the supplied KNN implementation, not the other problems in the document. Its insertion-based neighbor maintenance costs O(Nk). Measurements strongly favor changing that algorithm: baseline 2.02324 s; rejection-only 2.00979 s; NEON insertion scans 0.80123/0.72875 s; compact serial heap 0.02675 s; earlier parallel heap 0.02716 s; complement-selection/histogram C variant 0.02457 s, about 82x faster than baseline. C is the measured incumbent, but its roughly 8% advantage over A does not establish a threading benefit, and no integration measurements or timing breakdown are supplied. Preserve reference float distances, earlier-encounter priority for equal distances, smallest plain-char label on vote ties, and (char)-1 placeholder votes when k>N. NaNs require the reference's insertion behavior rather than an invented total ordering. Infinities and signed zeros must retain comparison semantics. Research should improve the heap family, isolate individual effects, and avoid assumptions about test values or input distributions."
}